# Narrowly scoped to artifacts/: preserved evidence must stay byte-exact on every
# platform. Without this, core.autocrlf rewrites the line endings on checkout and
# every recorded SHA-256 stops matching -- including the verified_full_report
# bytes the web app serves and checks against its own export_meta.json.
#
# This was a live bug, not a hypothetical: on a fresh Windows clone of v6.0.0,
# tests/test_web.py::test_verified_full_served_bytes_match_recorded_evidence_hashes
# fails, because artifacts/verified_full_report/analysis.json checks out as CRLF
# (8a950cad...) instead of the recorded 12d47b35.... It passed only in the working
# copy where the report generator had written the file directly.
#
# `binary` is `-text -diff -merge`: it pins the bytes AND stops Git from reading the
# preserved CR line endings as trailing whitespace, which would make `git diff --check`
# fail on every line of frozen evidence. These files are never hand-edited, so losing
# textual diffs on them costs nothing.
#
# This deliberately does NOT change the project's text rules for any other path.
artifacts/** binary
